# Expectation record for 12_preprocessor/002_conditional_compilation.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 002_conditional_compilation
area               = 12_preprocessor
description        = Nested conditional compilation with defined(), #ifdef/#ifndef, integer arithmetic in #if controlling expressions, and provably skipped groups
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction, which is the precondition that
makes a divergence readable as evidence about a compiler at all: a program containing
undefined behaviour licenses either compiler to do anything, so a difference between them
would prove nothing about either.

Preprocessor arithmetic. Every controlling expression is built from small integer constants
that the preprocessor evaluates as though every signed type had the representation of intmax_t
(C11 6.10.1p4), so no operation approaches overflow -- the largest value any of them computes
is 42, and the largest literal operand anywhere in the file is 64. The single shift, 1 << 4,
shifts a positive value by 4, a count strictly within range for every type in which it could
be evaluated: intmax_t in the preprocessor, and the 32-bit int all four targets provide had it
been translated. No negative value is ever shifted. The division -7 / 2 and the modulo 17 % 5
both have non-zero divisors; they assert truncation toward zero and a dividend-signed remainder,
which C99 onward mandates of every conforming implementation (C11 6.5.5p6), so the results are
fixed by the language rather than by the target. Both are nevertheless identical on all four
targets in fact as well as in principle, which is why no target is narrowed and all three
oracles stay enabled.

An undefined identifier in a #if is DEFINED behaviour, not undefined behaviour. C11 6.10.1p4
requires that after macro expansion and the defined operator have been applied, every remaining
identifier -- including one lexically identical to a keyword -- be replaced with the pp-number
zero. The controlling expression NOT_DEFINED_ANYWHERE == 0 && !defined(NOT_DEFINED_ANYWHERE)
therefore has a value the standard fixes, and pairing the arithmetic half with the defined()
half proves both halves of the rule at once. -Wundef is deliberately not a member of the default
warning gate, so the construct is gate-clean as written; it is also not a constraint violation,
so no diagnostic is required of any conforming implementation.

#undef of a macro that was never defined is legal. C11 6.10.3.5p2 states that such a directive
is ignored rather than diagnosed, so the #undef FEATURE_B line must compile silently. It is
present on purpose: it makes FEATURE_B undefined at every use below independently of anything
that precedes it, so the #ifndef arm the program takes cannot be perturbed by an edit above.

The one #error directive is unreachable by construction. It sits inside a #if 0 group, which a
conforming preprocessor must skip without evaluating, so this program compiling at all is the
assertion -- there is no output line for it to produce. No #error and no #warning appears on any
live path, so nothing is written to standard error, which this suite captures into finding
artifacts but never compares, because diagnostic wording legitimately differs between
compilers.

Runtime code. The single object, dead_marker, is initialised to 0 at its declaration and read
in the final printf, so there is no uninitialised read and no unused object. Every other
printed value is an integer macro resolved entirely at translation time. No pointer, array or
aggregate exists, so there is no aliasing violation, no out-of-bounds access, no one-past-end
pointer, and no dependence on padding bytes or on the addresses of unrelated objects. No object
is modified twice between sequence points, and no argument of any call has a side effect, so
nothing depends on unspecified evaluation order. No directive appears inside a function-call
argument list; every conditional is resolved at file scope into a plain integer macro, which
keeps each call a single well-formed expression. printf is hand-declared with a prototype
matching its use and every %d receives an int.

No header is included, and printf is hand-declared for that reason. bcc bundles only the
required freestanding headers and ships no <stdio.h> -- a search for "stdio" across the two
authoritative implementation documents, docs/project-guide.md and docs/technical-specifications.md,
returns no match. The claim is scoped to those two on purpose: the term does appear elsewhere
under docs/, in this suite's own methodology page docs/testing/differential-conformance.md,
which states this very conclusion and so cannot be evidence for it. So an #include <stdio.h>
would succeed under the reference compiler and fail under bcc, a spurious divergence caused by
the test rather than by the compiler. The one sanctioned header exception in this area is program
003, the dedicated bundled-header probe, and this is not it.

Determinism. Output is a fixed seven-line sequence, one line per preprocessing property
claimed, so a single divergent line localizes the defect to one construct. Only int values are
printed and always with %d, so neither the measured plain-char signedness difference nor the
measured i686 width difference can be observed. No address or pointer value is printed. No
__DATE__, __TIME__ or __FILE__ reference appears. There is no randomness and no locale-dependent
formatting, statement order is fixed throughout, and the exit status is 0, inside the permitted
0-125 range. The program is hermetic: every input is a literal in this source, and nothing is
opened, allocated or read from the environment.

The strongest observable in the program asserts an ABSENCE. A skipped group containing a nested
group whose own condition is true must leave dead_marker at 0; a preprocessor that failed to
skip the outer group would leave it at 1 or 2 and dead_block_skipped would print 0. That is
precisely the shape of defect a structural token-stream test is weakest at detecting and an
output oracle is strongest at.

No deviation from the default warning gate is requested, and none is sanctioned for this area.
The default gate (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror)
produces zero diagnostics in the single native compile-only invocation the suite makes of it;
the sanitizer gate (-fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all) builds, runs to
completion and exits 0 with nothing on standard error in its one instrumented native build;
and all twelve cells of the declared matrix produce byte-identical stdout with exit status 0
and an empty standard error.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Every construct exercised here is documented as supported - docs/technical-specifications.md
lines 93, 94 and 493 name #ifdef, #ifndef, #if, #elif, #else and #endif evaluation and the
preprocessor constant-expression evaluator with integer arithmetic and defined(), and
docs/project-guide.md's "C11 Frontend -- Preprocessor" row lists the same - so this program
carries no
expected-divergence marker and a divergence under any oracle is a genuine finding.

The measured target differences are handled by construction, so this program needs no
target restriction and no marker:

1. sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) are 4 on i686 and 8 on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64
   (docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462). No long, no size_t, no ptrdiff_t
   and no pointer value is printed anywhere, and no length modifier for any of them is
   used, so the difference cannot reach the output.
2. Plain char signedness is implementation-defined and was measured signed on x86_64 and
   i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. No plain char value is printed.
3. long double has three representations across the four targets (measured 16, 12, 16 and
   16 bytes, x87 80-bit against IEEE binary128). No long double appears in this program;
   that type is covered by 13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted, which is
   the only program permitted to narrow a comparison on its account.
4. All four targets are little-endian, and no byte-order-sensitive value is printed.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
nested_result=7
feature_a_on=1
feature_b_on=0
pp_arith_ok=1
undef_is_zero=1
width_in_range=1
dead_block_skipped=1
END
